Object-Relational Mapping

    .it addresses the bridge between the OOP approach and relational databases
    .useful in data interaction simplification, code optimization, and smooth blending of applications and databases 


ORDBMS 
    .enhances the functionalities of a relational database by incorporating object-oriented principles 
    .deals with complex data types, encapsulation, and data types 
    .supports applications that require both relational and object-oriented abilities 


Entities
    .synonymous with the objects or classes in object-oriented programming that are bound to the tables in 
    relational DBs 
    .serve as abstractions of business objects or the concepts within the application, and their definition is in the code
        .ORM component carries out the transformation of these entities into DB tables
        .it provides smooth communication between the application and the database beneath it 


